"# What I done with Bobby in Unity tonight\n- Added a crouching script, so Bobby can sneak\n- Made prefabs for the player and ai versions of Bobby\n- Set up a new scene and deleted the old sample one\n\t- Lots of chessboard patterns\n\t- Lots of big blocks\n\t- Some balls rolling around\n\t- Reflections and light probes \\(the latter mostly to contrast the interior of the conference room below\\)\n\t- Filled it with 8 wandering AI Brians\\. \n- Brought in the lab scan to walk around in\n- Brought in the conference room Scan to walk around in\n\t- Because it was a “watertight” scan with full walls and ceiling, I made it an enclosed room\n\t- And then I had to learn what was up with lighting and exposure here\\. \n\t\t- The translucent parts of the skin light up in the dark room\\. That doesn’t seem good\\. \n\t\t- Unity’s just adding dynamic exposure levels that react to visible lighting, and physically based skies, and post processing stacks, etc etc now\\. And I don’t know how I feel about that\\. \n- Redid the camera script, made the camera get blocked by colliders\n- Added a script that makes Bobby look where the cam is pointing\\. \n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/1A00E96AE046421389E10F93B5548F28)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/F3B180D6AAC441A182F9309AF0B71534)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/AFBDBFA74A2146818398BD1EE176FFBF)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/7331880939C84DD3BB0F1471B1B562D6)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/BF9246AE42E54FFD8A021560D9A08D5E)\n\n![](dayone-moment:\/\/B7933864E1324247A779D38D7429EC47)"
